---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const toc = [
  { id: "program", label: "Program description" },
  { id: "opt-in", label: "How you opt in" },
  { id: "frequency", label: "Frequency and cost" },
  { id: "opt-out", label: "How to opt out" },
  { id: "help", label: "Help" },
  { id: "examples", label: "Example messages" },
  { id: "carriers", label: "Carrier disclaimer" },
  { id: "privacy", label: "Privacy" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact" },
];
---

<Legal
  title="SMS Terms"
  description={`SMS Terms for ${site.name}: how to opt in, message frequency, rates, and how to opt out with STOP or get help with HELP.`}
  updated={site.legal.smsUpdated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="program">
    <h2>Program description</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} sends text messages to people who have asked to receive them.
      The program name is “{site.sms.programName}.” Messages may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A link to the website we built for your business, and a short video walkthrough of it, when you ask us to send one</li>
      <li>Replies to questions and inquiries you send us</li>
      <li>Scheduling messages</li>
      <li>A limited number of follow-up messages about the website you asked about</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not send messages to anyone who has not opted in, and we do not buy, sell, or rent phone number lists.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="opt-in">
    <h2>How you opt in</h2>
    <h3>On our website</h3>
    <p>
      You can opt in by checking the optional, unchecked-by-default text message consent box on our
      <a href="/#start">“Show me my site” form</a> (also on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>) and providing
      your mobile number. Checking the box is not required to submit the form.
    </p>
    <h3>By phone</h3>
    <p>
      During a phone call with {site.name}, a business owner may ask to receive a text message with a link to a video
      walkthrough of a website we've prepared for their business. Our representative uses this script:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      “Would you like me to text you a link to a five-minute video walkthrough of the site?” <em>(If yes:)</em> “What's
      the best mobile number to text it to? You'll get a text from Dimension Seven Systems to confirm, then the video
      once it's ready. Message and data rates may apply, and you can reply STOP at any time to opt out.”
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      We text only people who say yes and give us a mobile number. We record the date, time, and number of each verbal
      opt-in, and we send a confirmation text right after the call.
    </p>
    <p class="notice">Consent to receive text messages is not a condition of any purchase.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="frequency">
    <h2>Message frequency and cost</h2>
    <p>
      Message frequency varies depending on your request, and is typically a few messages per inquiry. Message and data
      rates may apply, depending on your mobile carrier plan.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="opt-out">
    <h2>How to opt out</h2>
    <p>
      Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any message at any time to stop receiving texts. You will receive one final message
      confirming that you have been unsubscribed, and no further messages will be sent. You can also opt out by calling
      or emailing us. To opt back in, reply <strong>START</strong>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="help">
    <h2>Help</h2>
    <p>
      Reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any message for help, or contact us at
      <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a> or <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="examples">
    <h2>Example messages</h2>
    <blockquote>
      Dimension Seven Systems: Thanks for chatting, Alex! We'll text your website walkthrough video here once it's
      ready. Msg &amp; data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help, STOP to opt out.
    </blockquote>
    <blockquote>
      Dimension Seven Systems: Hi Alex, here's the walkthrough of the new site for Sweet Tea Cleaning Co. we talked
      about: https://sweet-tea-demo.callcatcher.site Reply STOP to opt out.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      Website and walkthrough links point to a page on callcatcher.site, where we host the sites we build. See a
      <a href={site.demoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">sample site</a> (fictional business).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="carriers">
    <h2>Carrier disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Mobile carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p class="notice">
      No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. Text
      messaging originator opt-in data and consent will not be shared with any third parties.
    </p>
    <p>
      See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle your information, and our
      <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
